    {
      "id": "ge7eua8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LOCAL GOVERNMENT IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act established constitutional status for Panchayati Raj Institutions in rural India.",
        "The 74th Constitutional Amendment Act provided constitutional recognition to Urban Local Bodies.",
        "The Panchayati Raj system follows a three-tier structure: Gram Panchayat at the village level, Panchayat Samiti at the block level, and Zila Parishad at the district level.",
        "Gram Sabha serves as the foundational body consisting of all registered voters in the village area.",
        "Urban local bodies comprise Municipal Corporations, Municipal Councils, and Nagar Panchayats based on area size and population."
      ],
      "id": "bjk0jl6"
    },
